neuro Changes
=============

v0.2.0 -- Writing support and FreeSurfer annotation (parcellation) support
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEW:
- Add support for writing FreeSurfer surface files, function `WriteFsSurface`. This allows roundtrip support for the surface format.
- Add support for writing FreeSurfer MGH and MGZ files, function `WriteFsMgh`. The MGZ format is just gzip-compressed MGH format.
- Add support for writing FreeSurfer ASCII label files, function `WriteFsLabel`. This allows roundtrip support for the label format.
- Add support for reading and writing FreeSurfer annotation files (brain surface parcellations), functions `ReadFsAnnot` and `WriteFsAnnot`. This includes support for the color table and the Desikan-Killiany atlas (e.g., file `label/lh.aparc.annot`).
- The new `Annot` and `Colortable` data structures come with convenience methods, including `Annot.VertexColors` (per-vertex RGB(A) colors), `Annot.VertexRegionNames`, `Annot.VertexRegions`, `Annot.RegionVerticesByName`, and `Annot.RegionVerticesByLabel`.

FIXED: none
CHANGED: none

v0.1.3 -- Security release
---------------------------
This is a security release to fix the following security issue in a dependency:

Dependency: golang.org/x/net dependency
Vulnerable versions: < 0.13.0
Upgrade to: 0.13.0
Defined in: go.mod
Vulnerabilities:  CVE-2023-3978 (Moderate severity)  CVE-2023-39325 (Moderate severity)  CVE-2023-44487 (Moderate severity)


v0.1.2 -- Support for reading Freesurfer label files
----------------------------------------------------
NEW:
- Add support for reading labels, function `ReadFsLabel`.
FIXED: none
CHANGED: none


v0.1.1 -- Improved docs and Mgh struct fix
------------------------------------------
NEW:
- Add lots of documentation, including more detailed doc strings and a full MGH/MGZ demo application.
- Add a changelog in file CHANGES (this file)

FIXED:
- The `Mgh` struct now has public fields `Header` and `Data`, instead of private fields `header` and `data`.

CHANGED:
- The parameter `isGzipped` of functions `ReadFsMgh`, `ReadFsMghHeader` and `ReadFsMghData` now additionally accepts the strings `'mgh'` (alias for `'no'`) and `'mgz'` (alias for `'yes'`). This change is backwards compatible.


Version 0.1.0 -- Initial release
--------------------------------
- Support for reading FreeSurfer curv file format
- Support for writing FreeSurfer curv file format
- Support for reading FreeSurfer MGH file format
- Support for reading FreeSurfer MGZ file format
- Support for reading FreeSurfer surface file format (brain meshes)
- Support for computation of some simple mesh properties
